%N A401672 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) = n^2 + k^2 + n*k + n + k, 1 <= k <= n.
%C A401672 T(n,k) is the sum of the complete homogeneous symmetric polynomials of degrees 1 and 2 in n and k; i.e., T(n,k) = h_1(n,k) + h_2(n,k).
%C A401672 The polynomial is symmetric in n and k; only the lower triangular part is listed.
%H A401672 Eddie Lin Rui, <a href="/A401672/b401672.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10011</a> (first 141 rows, flattened)
%H A401672 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/CompleteHomogeneousSymmetricPolynomial.html">Complete Homogeneous Symmetric Polynomial</a>.
%e A401672 The triangle begins:
%e A401672    5;
%e A401672   10, 16;
%e A401672   17, 24, 33;
%e A401672   26, 34, 44,  56;
%e A401672   37, 46, 57,  70,  85;
%e A401672   50, 60, 72,  86, 102, 120;
%e A401672   65, 76, 89, 104, 121, 140, 161;
%e A401672 ...
%e A401672 T(4,2) = 4^2 + 2^2 + 4*2 + 4 + 2 = 16 + 4 + 8 + 4 + 2 = 34.
%o A401672 (Python)
%o A401672 def T(n, k):
%o A401672     return n**2 + k**2 + n*k + n + k
%o A401672 a = []
%o A401672 for n in range(1, 11):
%o A401672     a.extend(T(n, k) for k in range(1, n + 1))
%o A401672 print(a)
%Y A401672 Cf. A108872 (h_1).
%Y A401672 Cf. A215631, A132111 (h_2).
